<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jaghbub</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Al Jaghbub</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jaghbub is an oasis in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> near the Egyptian border. In 1856 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senussi-order">Senussi order</a> moved its headquarters there, and its founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-ali-al-senussi">Muhammad ibn Ali al-Senussi</a> was buried in its mosque. The oasis was transferred from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> to Italian Libya in 1925 and was besieged during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jaghbub.jpg" alt="Jaghbub" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ministry of War Office Propaganda, Rome 1941. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oasi_giarabub.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
